  "worked_solution": "A function is not differentiable wherever it has a discontinuity, corner, cusp, or vertical tangent.\n\n- At $x=-4$ the function has a corner point, so it's not differentiable there.\n\n- At $x=-2$ the function has a jump discontinuity, so it's not differentiable there.\n\nOf these two points, $f(x)$ is continuous only at $x=-4.$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is continuous but not differentiable at $x=-4.$",
